...FLOOD ADVISORY IN EFFECT UNTIL 10 PM EDT THIS EVENING...



* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.



* WHERE...A portion of western North Carolina, including the 

  following counties, Buncombe, Henderson and Transylvania.



* WHEN...Until 1000 PM EDT.



* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas. 



* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...

  - At 802 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to

    thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin

    shortly in the advisory area. Between 1.5 and 3 inches of

    rain have fallen.

  - Additional rainfall amounts of 0.3 to 0.6 inches are expected

    over the area. This additional rain will result in minor

    flooding.

