/O.NEW.KOAX.SV.W.0188.250730T0025Z-250730T0115Z/



BULLETIN - IMMEDIATE BROADCAST REQUESTED

Severe Thunderstorm Warning

National Weather Service Omaha/Valley Nebraska

725 PM CDT Tue Jul 29 2025



The National Weather Service in Omaha has issued a



* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...

  Western Knox County in northeastern Nebraska...



* Until 815 PM CDT.



* At 724 PM CDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line

  extending from near Tripp to 6 miles northeast of Verdel to 11

  miles north of Page, moving east at 30 mph.



  HAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and nickel size hail.



  SOURCE...Radar indicated.



  IMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.



* Severe thunderstorms will be near...

  Niobrara around 730 PM CDT.

  Verdigre around 740 PM CDT.



Other locations in the path of these severe thunderstorms include

Santee, Winnetoon and Center.



PRECAUTIONARY/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...



For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a

building.



Torrential rainfall is occurring with these storms, and may lead to

flash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.



&&



LAT...LON 4284 9819 4284 9815 4276 9804 4277 9795

      4279 9791 4282 9788 4286 9788 4287 9785

      4285 9778 4285 9773 4251 9790 4251 9830

      4288 9830

TIME...MOT...LOC 0024Z 275DEG 26KT 4324 9798 4289 9810 4256 9834 



HAIL THREAT...RADAR INDICATED

MAX HAIL SIZE...0.88 IN

WIND THREAT...RADAR INDICATED

MAX WIND GUST...60 MPH



$$



